<% content_for :page_title, 'Campaign content & review' %>
<main class="sales-workspace growth-workspace">
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag '/lightek/sales-workspace.css?v=4' %><%= stylesheet_link_tag '/lightek/growth-workspace.css?v=3' %>
  <%= render 'dashboard/shared/business_workspace', active: 'Campaigns' %>
  <p><%= link_to 'Attach a Studio export / open publishing calendar', dashboard_publication_calendar_path(site_id: @site.id, campaign_id: @campaign.id) if @campaign.channel == 'social' %></p>
  <header class="sales-header"><div><span class="sales-eyebrow">NEVAEH / CREATE · REVIEW · DELIVER</span><h1>Campaign content & review</h1><p><%= @campaign.name %> · <%= @campaign.channel.humanize %></p></div><%= link_to 'Back to campaign', edit_dashboard_marketing_campaign_path(@campaign, site_id: @site.id), class: 'sales-button secondary' %></header>
  <% if flash[:alert] %><div class="sales-errors" role="alert"><%= flash[:alert] %></div><% end %><% if flash[:notice] %><p role="status"><%= flash[:notice] %></p><% end %>
  <section class="sales-panel"><h2>Prepare three approaches</h2><p>Offer, problem and benefit variations use the shared Nevaeh writing engine with reviewed business facts. Review every claim, tone and call to action before approving. These are copy drafts, not finished media.</p>
    <%= form_with url: generate_dashboard_campaign_content_path(site_id: @site.id, campaign_id: @campaign.id), class: 'sales-form' do %><%= hidden_field_tag :request_key, SecureRandom.uuid %><label>Tracked call to action<%= select_tag :tracking_link_id, options_from_collection_for_select(@links, :id, :label), include_blank: 'Use current campaign URL (untracked unless already a tracking URL)' %></label><%= submit_tag 'Prepare content variations', class: 'sales-button' %><% end %>
    <p><%= link_to 'Review business brief and tracking links', dashboard_growth_path(site_id: @site.id) %></p>
  </section>
  <p>Delivery context: <strong><%= @campaign.channel.humanize %></strong> · sender <%= @sender_address.presence || 'Not selected' %> · recipient <%= @campaign.recipient_email.presence || 'Subscribed audience / selected social destination' %>. Start: <%= @campaign.starts_at&.to_fs(:long) || 'Unscheduled' %>.</p>
  <section class="sales-coach"><span class="sales-eyebrow">CURRENT CAMPAIGN REVIEW</span><p><%= @campaign.content_review_required? ? (@campaign.content_approved? ? "Approved #{@campaign.content_approved_at.to_fs(:long)}. Changes to the approved payload invalidate this review." : 'Content changed. Review and approve a fresh content set before publishing.') : 'This campaign uses the existing Ready workflow. Approving a variation enrolls it in version-specific content review.' %></p><p><%= link_to 'Open campaign editor / Studio', edit_dashboard_marketing_campaign_path(@campaign, site_id: @site.id) %> · <% if current_user.role.in?(%w[admin super_admin]) %><%= link_to 'Open existing publishing tools', dashboard_social_connections_path(site_id: @site.id) %><% else %>Social publication uses the existing authorized publishing operator.<% end %></p></section>
  <% if @variants.empty? %><p class="sales-empty">Prepare the first set to compare different ways of presenting the offer.</p><% end %>
  <% @variants.each do |variant| %><article class="sales-panel growth-content-variant"><span class="sales-eyebrow"><%= variant.angle.humanize %> / <%= variant.status.humanize %> / COPY REVISION <%= variant.lock_version %></span><h2><%= variant.headline %></h2><p><small>Prepared <%= variant.created_at.to_fs(:long) %> · brief revision <%= variant.source_snapshot['brief_revision'] %> · <%= variant.source_snapshot['writer_version'] %></small></p>
    <details class="growth-plan-evidence"><summary>Writing context and applied direction</summary><p>Voice: <%= variant.source_snapshot.dig('brief', 'voice') %></p><p>Audience: <%= variant.source_snapshot.dig('brief', 'audience') %></p><p>Goal: <%= variant.source_snapshot.dig('brief', 'goal') %></p><pre><%= JSON.pretty_generate(variant.source_snapshot['editorial']) %></pre><p><small>The writer reports supported and unsupported direction. It does not promise arbitrary brand-voice understanding.</small></p></details>
    <% if variant.status == 'draft' %><%= form_with url: dashboard_campaign_content_variant_path(site_id: @site.id, campaign_id: @campaign.id, id: variant.id), method: :patch, scope: :variant, class: 'sales-form' do |f| %><%= hidden_field_tag :lock_version, variant.lock_version %><label>Headline<%= f.text_field :headline, value: variant.headline, maxlength: 200, required: true %></label><label>Copy<%= f.text_area :message, value: variant.message, rows: 8, maxlength: 8000, required: true %></label><div class="sales-form-grid"><label>Call to action<%= f.text_field :cta_label, value: variant.cta_label, maxlength: 60, required: true %></label><label>Call to action URL<%= f.url_field :cta_url, value: variant.cta_url, maxlength: 400, required: true %></label></div><label>Media URL<%= f.url_field :media_url, value: variant.media_url, maxlength: 1200 %></label><%= f.submit 'Save draft revision', class: 'sales-button secondary' %><% end %>
      <%= form_with url: approve_dashboard_campaign_content_variant_path(site_id: @site.id, campaign_id: @campaign.id, id: variant.id), class: 'sales-form growth-step-resolution' do %><%= hidden_field_tag :lock_version, variant.lock_version %><label><%= check_box_tag :confirmed, '1', false, required: true %> I reviewed the saved copy, claims, audience, channel, media and call to action for this version.</label><p><small>Save edits before approving. Approval applies the saved version and marks the campaign ready; it does not publish.</small></p><%= submit_tag 'Approve & use this version', class: 'sales-button' %><% end %>
    <% else %><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"><%= variant.message %></p><p><%= variant.cta_label %> · <%= variant.cta_url %></p><p>Approved <%= variant.approved_at.to_fs(:long) %> by <%= variant.approved_by.email_address %>. This saved version is immutable.</p><% end %>
  </article><% end %>
  <p><small>Latest 30 variations. A changed brief or campaign requires a fresh set. Campaigns with delivery/publication history require a separate campaign for new approved copy. Existing Studio productions retain edits when reopened; a new production seeds the current campaign copy.</small></p>
</main>
